l-.707.707M6.343 17.657l-.707.707M16 12a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0z\" class=\"jsx-e342f6f6474abc3a\"></path></svg></button><button style=\"display:none;background:none;border:none;color:var(--text);font-size:24px;cursor:pointer\" aria-label=\"Menu\" class=\"jsx-2732561215c3f3d nav-toggle-btn\">☰</button></div></header><main class=\"flex-1\"><!--$!--><template data-dgst=\"BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING\"></template><div class=\"cat-strip-outer\"><div class=\"cat-strip\">Loading categories…</div></div><!--/$--><main class=\"container mx-auto px-4 py-6\"><nav class=\"breadcrumbs text-sm\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><ul><li><a class=\"text-base-content/60 hover:text-primary\" href=\"/\">Home</a></li><li><span class=\"text-base-content font-medium\">News</span></li></ul></nav><h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold mt-4 mb-1\">Latest tech news</h1><p class=\"text-base-content/60 mb-5\">Fresh phone, laptop &amp; gadget news, refreshed daily from across the web.</p><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-6\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-primary\">All</button><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline\">electronics</button><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline\">cameras</button><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline\">auto</button><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline\">mobiles</button><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline\">tech</button><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline\">tvs</button><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline\">monitors</button><button class=\"btn btn-sm btn-outline\">routers</button></div><div class=\"grid gap-5\" style=\"grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr))\"><a href=\"https://www.xda-developers.com/astros-a-distro-that-combines-the-best-of-arch-cosmic-and-immutability-enters-beta/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://static0.xdaimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/astros-logo.jpg\" alt=\"AstrOS, a distro that combines the best of Arch, COSMIC, and immutability, enters beta\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">electronics</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">AstrOS, a distro that combines the best of Arch, COSMIC, and immutability, enters beta</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">You&#x27;ll need a TPM 2.0 CPU for this one</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">XDA Developers</span><time dateTime=\"2026-08-01\">5 hours ago</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.techradar.com/pro/zelensky-confirms-ukraines-drones-will-reach-6-000-miles-in-2027-enough-to-cover-the-entirety-of-russia-and-able-to-reach-as-far-as-san-francisco-from-kyiv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rpDiL2aBWBfnfUJ6QVXfnd-1280-80.png\" alt=\"Zelensky confirms Ukraine&#x27;s drones will reach 6,000 miles in 2027 — enough to cover the entirety of Russia and able to reach as far as San Francisco from Kyiv\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">cameras</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">Zelensky confirms Ukraine&#x27;s drones will reach 6,000 miles in 2027 — enough to cover the entirety of Russia and able to reach as far as San Francisco from Kyiv</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">Ukraine plans longer-range drones reaching 10,000 km by 2027 while pursuing US cooperation for production, testing, and advanced unmanned technology development.</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">TechRadar</span><time dateTime=\"2026-08-01\">5 hours ago</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.xda-developers.com/windows-has-been-quietly-wearing-out-your-ssd-and-the-fix-takes-one-setting/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://static0.xdaimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/wm/2026/07/crucial-ssd-desktop.jpg\" alt=\"Windows has been quietly wearing out your SSD, and the fix takes one setting\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">auto</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">Windows has been quietly wearing out your SSD, and the fix takes one setting</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">Microsoft wouldn&#x27;t take care of my storage, so I will</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">XDA Developers</span><time dateTime=\"2026-08-01\">5 hours ago</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/07/31/gemini-ai-studio-app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://picsum.photos/seed/8804/600/340\" alt=\"Gemini will create mobile &amp; desktop apps in the future as AI Studio for Android, iOS is canceled\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">mobiles</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">Gemini will create mobile &amp; desktop apps in the future as AI Studio for Android, iOS is canceled</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">At I/O 2026, Google teased an AI Studio app for Android and iOS. This mobile application has been canceled in favor of what sounds like a deep Gemini app integration.</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">9to5Google</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.xda-developers.com/amd-promised-am5-support-until-2029-and-the-memory-crisis-might-not-let-it-stop-there/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://static0.xdaimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/wm/2024/11/amd-ryzen-7-9800x3d-installed.jpg\" alt=\"AMD promised AM5 support until 2029, and the memory crisis might not let it stop there\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">tech</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">AMD promised AM5 support until 2029, and the memory crisis might not let it stop there</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">AM5 is now the past, present, and apparently, the future for consumer PCs</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">XDA Developers</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.techradar.com/pro/grab-1-54tb-free-cloud-storage-for-life-but-you-will-need-to-sign-up-43-services\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/E4uAqGFTRWwta845DHU8z9-1280-80.jpg\" alt=\"Grab 1.54TB free cloud storage for life — but you will need to sign up to 43 services\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">tech</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">Grab 1.54TB free cloud storage for life — but you will need to sign up to 43 services</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">No strings attached, but you will need to subscribe to and maintain more than 40 services.</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">TechRadar</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.techradar.com/computing/websites-apps/nyt-strands-today-answers-hints-1-august-2026\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/XrpFgcngWrtXQscKdLLAZB-1280-80.jpg\" alt=\"NYT Strands hints and answers for Saturday, August 1 (game #881)\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">electronics</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">NYT Strands hints and answers for Saturday, August 1 (game #881)</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">Looking for NYT Strands answers and hints? Here&#x27;s all you need to know to solve today&#x27;s game, including the spangram.</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">TechRadar</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.techradar.com/pro/seagate-reveals-more-on-its-50tb-hdd-plans-but-looks-like-well-still-have-a-long-wait-to-buy-one\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/aTFUiygNrf75WJgGpPiXvf-1280-80.jpeg\" alt=\"Seagate reveals more on its 50TB HDD plans — but looks like we&#x27;ll still have a long wait to buy one\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">tech</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">Seagate reveals more on its 50TB HDD plans — but looks like we&#x27;ll still have a long wait to buy one</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">Seagate&#x27;s 50TB hard drives finally have a date: qualification in late 2027, shipments in 2028.</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">TechRadar</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.xda-developers.com/moved-half-my-work-to-haiku-sonnet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://static0.xdaimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/wm/2026/07/claude-models-displayed-within-claude-code-cli-window.jpeg\" alt=\"I moved half my work to Haiku + Sonnet and couldn&#x27;t tell the difference for most of it\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">tech</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">I moved half my work to Haiku + Sonnet and couldn&#x27;t tell the difference for most of it</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">It&#x27;s me, hi, I&#x27;m the problem, it&#x27;s me</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">XDA Developers</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.xda-developers.com/esp32-robots-microblocks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://static0.xdaimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/microblocks-robot-featured.jpg\" alt=\"After five years of work, these ESP32 robots you can program in real time are ready for you to build\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">electronics</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">After five years of work, these ESP32 robots you can program in real time are ready for you to build</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">They&#x27;re also really cute.</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">XDA Developers</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/science/2026/07/not-ju