5k-1280-80.jpg\" alt=\"I&#x27;m incredibly excited for The Witcher 4 - but CD Projekt Red needs to avoid the same performance issues The Witcher 3 and Cyberpunk 2077 once had\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">tech</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">I&#x27;m incredibly excited for The Witcher 4 - but CD Projekt Red needs to avoid the same performance issues The Witcher 3 and Cyberpunk 2077 once had</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">The Witcher 4 is my most anticipated RPG, but I hope CDPR has learned its lesson from Cyberpunk 2077&#x27;s launch and prioritizes optimization over a massive world.</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">TechRadar</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/31/antizuck-ios-app-that-claims-to-detect-nearby-smart-glasses-tops-app-store-chart/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://picsum.photos/seed/23948/600/340\" alt=\"‘Antizuck’ iOS app that claims to detect nearby smart glasses tops App Store chart\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">mobiles</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">‘Antizuck’ iOS app that claims to detect nearby smart glasses tops App Store chart</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">Vibes around Meta’s AI glasses are off lately. So much so that one of the top three paid iPhone apps today is dedicated to detecting when someone nearby may be using smart glasses.</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">9to5Mac</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.techradar.com/vpn/vpn-privacy-security/first-your-age-next-your-identity-inside-the-hack-that-broke-the-eu-age-verification-apps-privacy-promises\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden bg-base-300\"><img src=\"https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/WSCXYRKEQTYxJyzZRF6ULb-1280-80.png\" alt=\"First your age, next your identity: Inside the &#x27;hack&#x27; that broke the EU age verification app&#x27;s privacy promises\" class=\"w-full h-full object-cover\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span class=\"absolute top-2 left-2 badge badge-md badge-primary\">tech</span></figure><div class=\"card-body p-4 gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-base font-semibold line-clamp-2 leading-snug\">First your age, next your identity: Inside the &#x27;hack&#x27; that broke the EU age verification app&#x27;s privacy promises</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-base-content/60 line-clamp-3\">The security expert who &#x27;hacked&#x27; the EU age verification continues to say that the &quot;concept cannot work&quot; — no matter the tech. If lawmakers keep going through, he fears that &quot;the next step will be pro</p><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/50\"><span class=\"font-medium\">TechRadar</span><time dateTime=\"2026-07-31\">Yesterday</time></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.androidauthority.com/google-pixel-watch-4-lte-amazon-deal-3693360/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" class=\"card bg-base-200 border border-base-300 hover:border-primary transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 duration-200\"><figure class=\"relative aspect-vid